			<div class="content" id="post-content-3738943">
									

<p>Absolutely stellar. I can't imagine how much work went into this, but it certainly paid off. +1</p>
<p>That said, I noticed some typos here and there, but I have no idea how to go about fixing them.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">One&nbsp;ongoing&nbsp;issue,&nbsp;though.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>When you end a piece of dialogue with a period, the following word should be capitalized. If the following words form a dependent clause, the dialogue should end with a comma.</p>
<p>So, this is correct:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Yes, sir, of course.&quot; The speed at which she speaks — as well as the fact that she's stood at your door in the first place — reveals her lie.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>But here&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Sally.&quot; you reply. &quot;Is everything okay?&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The period after &quot;Sally&quot; should be a comma. Even if the dialogue ends at &quot;Sally&quot;, &quot;you reply&quot; is technically part of the same sentence. The corrected form would thus read:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Sally,&quot; you reply. &quot;Is everything okay?&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>

